## Pitfall Alert

$CALLOUT$S?type=danger&title=Negative+Edge+Weights+Break+Dijkstra
Dijkstra assumes that once a node is marked visited, its shortest distance is finalized. A negative edge can retroactively decrease the distance to an already finalized node, producing incorrect results. Use **Bellman-Ford** or **Johnson's Algorithm** if edges can have negative weights.
$CALLOUT$E
